// Registry #942(b) — a peer's source location must name the PEER.
//
// Until 2026-09-05 it named the entry file. `CEmitter::loc_for_span` took a bare
// `span_start: usize`, so the file id was discarded at the door and the name came
// from a single `source_file_name` while the line was computed against the ENTRY
// file's text — wrong file and a line measured in the wrong document. Measured on
// this very corpus: a failing `assert` in `append_as_slice.nv:6` announced itself
// as `a_q3_println_debug_record.nv:2`.
//
// That is not a cosmetic defect. A runtime location is what a person opens when
// something breaks, and one that points confidently at an unrelated file sends
// them to read code that has nothing to do with their failure.
//
// WHY THIS FIXTURE ASSERTS A LOCATION RATHER THAN PROVOKING A FAILURE: the honest
// carrier is a FAILING assertion, and a fixture cannot fail on purpose and stay
// green. `caller_loc()` (D468) hands the same machinery's answer to a passing
// test — it goes through `loc_for_span_raw`, the identical resolver `assert` and
// contract violations use, so pinning it here pins theirs.
//
// It lives as an ordinary peer of `spec_tests/conformance` on purpose: the defect
// exists ONLY inside a multi-peer compile unit, and this CU has 1177 of them. A
// standalone file could not reproduce it — it is its own entry, so the wrong
// answer and the right one coincide.
//
// Spec: D468 (`caller_loc`), D29 (folder-module peers).
module spec_tests.conformance

fn p942_where_am_i() -> CallerLoc => caller_loc()

test "942: a peer's caller_loc names the peer, not the entry file" {
    ro loc = p942_where_am_i()
    // The entry of this CU is `a_q3_println_debug_record.nv` (alphabetically
    // first), which is exactly the name this used to report.
    assert(loc.file == "p942_peer_caller_loc.nv")
    // Line 28 is `fn p942_where_am_i()` above — `caller_loc()` written plainly in
    // a body means HERE (D468), so it is the declaration's own line, not this
    // call's. Pinned to a number so that a location computed against another
    // file's text cannot pass by accident: it would have to land on 28 there too.
    assert(loc.line == 28)
}
